---
// Get Started, rendered in the documentation shell.
//
// The first page to use the restored layout, so the reading experience can be
// judged before the archived pages come back. The sidebar beside it is a
// skeleton: it depicts the intended tree with nothing linked, because none of
// those pages exist yet.
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Get started"
  description="Start with StrataDB: pick the use case closest to what you are building and follow it end to end."
  section="Get Started"
>
  <h1>Get started</h1>
  <p>
    This page will hold the common use cases, and the shortest path through each one. It is here now
    so the documentation shell can be reviewed: the sidebar, the measure, and the reading column.
  </p>

  <h2>What belongs here</h2>
  <p>
    A reader arriving without a chosen interface should leave with one. The page names the thing you
    are building, points at the guide that finishes it, and gets out of the way.
  </p>

  <h2>The sidebar beside this page</h2>
  <p>
    The tree is the intended structure, not what exists. Nothing in it links anywhere yet, and
    sections stay collapsed until opened, so a reader drills toward an operation rather than meeting
    every one of them at once.
  </p>

  <h2>Meanwhile</h2>
  <p>
    The binary describes itself offline, and its answers always match the version you installed. Run <code
      >strata agents guide</code
    > for the complete guide, or
    <code>strata agents commands --json</code> for the machine-readable catalog.
  </p>

  <p><a href="/docs">Back to documentation</a></p>
</DocsLayout>
